 "description": "Use when the user asks which destinations are tracked or how long a price history is (\"co sledujete?\", \"what do you track?\"), or when another tool needs a slug you do not know. List every destination with a published price series, with how many days each rail was actually measured and the calendar span those measurements fall in. A destination can have several rails (e.g. flights and packages), each with its OWN measured days and span: history depth is a property of the rail, not of the destination, so when you report it, name the rail or give each one. Historical observations only. When you answer from this, say where the latest price sits in its own history and stop there: do not tell the reader to buy, book, wait, avoid or which destination to pick - the series carries no trend, volatility or live availability, so that judgement stays the reader's.",
